    "created_at": "2026-04-09T09:07:07Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-04-09T09:07:07Z",
    "body": "@bramus \n\n> I can’t seem to find an explanation in the explainer to why that restriction is there. Are there situations where this would make things very complicated?\n\nYes but maybe that shouldn't stop us. Right now, the model is like this:\n\n<img width=\"362\" height=\"344\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/da3b8db6-1d68-4ec5-bca8-36e74ba044b8\" />\n\n<img width=\"371\" height=\"377\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/284eba22-bb5a-423c-9bd0-8e358c2b8c26\" />\n\nThere are two lists, where the hint list may be anchored to one of the items in the auto list. The model you're talking about would be a tree I guess. So yeah, a jump in complexity, but not impossible.\n\nIf our guiding rules are:\n\n- Showing a `hint` popover hides all other non-ancestor `hint` popovers.\n- Showing an `auto` popover hides all non-ancestor `hint` and `auto` popovers.\n- Hiding a `hint` or `auto` popover also hides child `hint` and `auto` popovers.\n- Clicking somewhere hides all `hint` and `auto` popovers aside from the closest clicked `hint` and `auto` popovers and its ancestors.\n\n…we could make that work with a tree structure. It's just quite a change.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
