    "updated_at": "2026-04-09T09:12:12Z",
    "body": "@lukewarlow \n\n> Does it make sense turn a select popover into a popover=hint, does that break anything? I guess we _could_ define it as a manual and then define extra behaviour but that's probably not worth it.\n\nOne of the weirdness I encountered with `popover=hint` is that its interaction with `popopver=auto` would change in the nested situation, because to some degree the spec/implementation was 'upgrading' the nested hint to an auto. So I expect to some degree, the downgrade would seem weird if developers encountered it.\n\nFor example, it would mean that opening a sibling hint would close the select picker, which generally wouldn't happen, because hints don't close autos. But if they're both hints, then one would close the other.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
